{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Tcp.Keepalive</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"tcpip","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Tcpip","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Tcp","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Keepalive","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Configuration for TCP keep-alives. Keep-alive messages are probes sent on an idle connection. If no traffic is received after a certain number of probes are sent, then the connection is assumed to have been lost.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> t</span><span> = </span><span>{</span></code><ol><li id=\"type-t.after\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.after\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>after : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Duration</span>.t;</span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>initial delay before sending probes on an idle connection</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li><li id=\"type-t.interval\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.interval\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>interval : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Duration</span>.t;</span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>interval between successive probes</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li><li id=\"type-t.probes\" class=\"def record field anchored\"><a href=\"#type-t.probes\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>probes : int;</span></code><div class=\"def-doc\"><span class=\"comment-delim\">(*</span><p>total number of probes to send before assuming that, if the connection is still idle it has been lost</p><span class=\"comment-delim\">*)</span></div></li></ol><code><span>}</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Configuration for TCP keep-alives</p></div></div>"}